  "notes": [
    "<sandbox>/work in argv stands for a fresh scratch copy of this run's inputs/ folder, mounted at /w; the inputs are kept under inputs/ as they ran.",
    "Each log is the container's stdout followed by its stderr. verdict_lines are the lines of the log the recorder keeps (content/audit/tools/record-exemplars.mjs), copied in log order.",
    "<repo> in argv is the course repository at the commit the inputs' hashes name, mounted read-only at /r with PYTHONPATH=/r/bench, as RUN-sql-shape-validator and RUN-tlc-trace-validation mount it; inputs lists the files of it the run reads.",
    "reply.py imports the course's reference simulator, bench/statespace/sim.py, from the read-only mount; for q6 it replaces ReferenceMachine with a subclass whose step answers a reply with the block between the '--- q6' markers in reply.py, and leaves every other branch to the reference. labs/LAB-8/reference/ and labs/LAB-8/challenge/ under inputs/ are the files of RUN-tlc-trace-validation's inputs, copied verbatim, which statespace trace validate reads.",
    "The end-state suite is the agent's: after the run, c1 is acked, its result stored, and the provider charged it once. The monitor line is the harness's own describe() of the run, which checks NoDoubleCharge and AckedIsDurable while the run goes."
  ]
}
